# .mailmap - Git commit mapping
# Format: Proper Name <email@address.com> <commit-name> <commit-email@address.com>
# This file maps multiple commit identities to a single canonical identity.

# Example:
# John Doe <john@example.com> jd <jd@old-email.com>
# Jane Smith <jane@example.com> jsmith <jane@old-domain.com>
Adam Wan<adamaikenadam@gmail.com>
